Dataset attribution and separate license

The MIT terms above apply to our project code and original project
documentation. Samrómur Icelandic Speech 21.05 audio, release transcripts,
metadata, and derived scoring references use Creative Commons Attribution
4.0 International (CC BY 4.0).

Samrómur 21.05 creators are David Erik Mollberg, Ólafur Helgi Jónsson,
Sunneva Þorsteinsdóttir, Jóhanna Vigdís Guðmundsdóttir, Steinþór
Steingrímsson, Eydís Huld Magnúsdóttir, Judy Y. Fong, Michal Borsky,
and Jón Guðnason. The Language and Voice Lab at Reykjavík University
developed the corpus in cooperation with Almannarómur.

Release: https://repository.clarin.is/repository/xmlui/handle/20.500.12537/189
License: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
Publication: https://aclanthology.org/2020.lrec-1.425/

This repository selects and repackages unchanged published FLACs and uses
the release prompts to derive normalized scoring text. The original
prompt text and the complete published metadata are preserved.
